body:
An occupied deregistered prefix is treated as available here, but `copy_dir_all` never clears its `.lance-deregistered` marker. The method then deletes the source and returns success while namespace lookup still rejects the destination, leaving no readable name. Reject every existing destination prefix, or replace it through a staged/no-replace publication that cannot retain old marker state, before removing the source.

<details><summary>Reproducer run on this head</summary>

Added to the existing test module and ran `cargo test -p lance-namespace-impls gate_repro_rename_over_deregistered_destination_keeps_marker -- --nocapture`:

```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn gate_repro_rename_over_deregistered_destination_keeps_marker() {
    use lance_namespace::models::{DeregisterTableRequest, RenameTableRequest};

    let temp_dir = TempStdDir::default();
    let namespace = DirectoryNamespaceBuilder::new(temp_dir.to_str().unwrap())
        .manifest_enabled(false)
        .build()
        .await
        .unwrap();

    for name in ["source", "destination"] {
        let mut request = CreateTableRequest::new();
        request.id = Some(vec![name.to_string()]);
        namespace
            .create_table(request, Bytes::from(create_non_empty_test_ipc_data()))
            .await
            .unwrap();
    }

    let mut deregister = DeregisterTableRequest::new();
    deregister.id = Some(vec!["destination".to_string()]);
    namespace.deregister_table(deregister).await.unwrap();

    let mut rename = RenameTableRequest::new("destination".to_string());
    rename.id = Some(vec!["source".to_string()]);
    namespace.rename_table(rename).await.unwrap();

    let status = namespace.check_table_status("destination").await.unwrap();
    assert!(!status.is_deregistered);
}
```

The rename returned `Ok`, then the assertion failed because `is_deregistered` remained `true`; the source directory had already been removed.

</details>
